    {
      "id": "claim_6e87bd6aa1934058a189b66d6bad33a6",
      "statement": "A null paper_claimed_* field means the source paper reported win rates, t-statistics, or conditional-mean tables rather than a mechanical Sharpe or CAGR — common for technical-rule and book-sourced strategies — and not that the strategy is weak; the only performance claim stood behind in those cases is the post-gate one measured on internal data.",
