      "statement": "Several library strategies substitute a price-based proxy for data the engine does not have: cross-asset value proxies cheapness by deviation from a rolling mean, Quality Minus Junk collapses four accounting dimensions into a price-based information ratio, and the dividend-yield strategy is a high-D/P-sort proxy rather than a true dividend sort.",
